{
  "dom_id": "step-q91805",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Matt wants to distribute $5$ liters of white paint into containers, each having a capacity of $\\frac{1}{5}$ of a liter. How many containers will Matt need?",
  "worked_solution": "To determine how many containers Matt will need, we need to divide the amount of paint by the capacity of each container:\n\n$$\n5÷\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nTo divide a whole number by a unit fraction, we multiply the whole number by the fraction's denominator:\n\n$$\n5÷\\frac{1}{5}=5\\times 5=25\n$$",
